diff --git a/docs/internals/agent-session-import.md b/docs/internals/agent-session-import.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1665efc664
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/internals/agent-session-import.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Native agent-session import fidelity
+
+The session importer is deliberately a **native import**, not a legacy T3 database
+migration. It writes current v2 events and binds the imported provider thread to the
+original Claude, Codex, or OpenCode native session.
+
+## Fidelity contract
+
+| Area                     | Current behavior                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Evidence / boundary                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
+| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Native continuation      | Claude imports keep `nativeThreadRef` and resume that session on the first follow-up.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | On 2026-10-29, a copied 364 MB real session recalled an earlier conversation topic without tools. After restarting the built server, it recalled a different earlier discussion. Both protocol opens used `resume`, not `sessionId`. An exact `RESUME_OK` response alone does not establish retained context. |
+| Legacy handoff avoidance | Native imports use `historyOrigin: "native"`; `"v1_import"` would make the orchestrator create a legacy context handoff.                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | The first real continuation test failed through the handoff budget; changing the origin made direct native resume pass.                                                                                                                                                                                       |
+| Visible messages         | User and assistant text is imported into current v2 message and turn-item events.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Scanner/importer tests and isolated projection.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| Claude branch            | Only the current branch is imported. It is found on a parent graph of every main-chain record, because real sessions link prompts and replies through attachment, hook, and timing records the importer does not retain. The leaf is the latest visible message at or after Claude's `last-prompt` marker.                               | A walk over retained records alone stopped after 2–3 records on real sessions and fell back to the whole file, mixing abandoned branches in. The 364 MB session now imports its full 732-prompt branch.                                                                                                       |
+| Provider turns/nodes     | Historical provider turns and execution nodes are emitted with weak native item refs.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Isolated Claude projection: 9,780 nodes for the 364 MB session.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| Claude images            | Inline base64 Claude images are persisted under T3’s attachment store with deterministic IDs and attached to imported messages.                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Target transcript produced 51 persisted image files / 51 unique attachment payloads. Remote image URLs are not downloaded.                                                                                                                                                                                    |
+| Claude subagents         | Native `Agent`/`Task` calls produce subagent nodes, subagent projections, and subagent turn items with prompt/result/status/native task refs.                                                                                                                                                                                            | Target projection produced 24 subagents and 24 subagent turn items.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
+| Claude reasoning/tools   | Thinking blocks become reasoning items. Tool calls go through the live adapter's `claudeToolTurnItem` with the transcript's structured `toolUseResult`, so they render as live Claude tools do: command, file change, web search, or MCP-branded dynamic tool. Tool results are deduplicated by tool ID while reading large transcripts. | Importer test; target projection produced 2,654 command, 243 file change, 29 web search, and 304 dynamic tool items.                                                                                                                                                                                          |
+| Claude compaction        | Compact boundaries on the branch reconnect through `logicalParentUuid` (only toward an older record) and become `compaction` items on the next imported message.                                                                                                                                                                         | Scanner test; 13 of 13 boundaries in the target session.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
+| Codex native history     | Explicit `source: "codex"` reads full canonical items through app-server, including paginated turns and archived discovery. Commands, exit codes, file changes, plans, exposed reasoning, delegation and compaction use native IDs and terminal statuses.                                                                                | Synthetic parser/source/projection tests and isolated CLI 0.166.0 list/read/resume/restart checks.                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
+| OpenCode 2               | Explicit `source: "opencode"` reads complete session exports, excludes reverted messages, preserves ordered blocks and files, and pages shell output. Tools use the live OpenCode mapper.                                                                                                                                                | Synthetic tests and isolated OpenCode 2.0.28 list/export checks.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
+| Idempotency              | Re-importing an unchanged source is recognized as already imported; event IDs and attachment IDs are deterministic.                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Importer tests and repeated isolated imports.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
+| Restart durability       | v2 projection, provider binding, subagents, turns, and attachments survive server restart.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | Isolated restart query verified provider native ID, 2,335 turns, nodes, and attachments.                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
+
+## Intentional limits
+
+These are not silently treated as native parity:
+
+- Claude currently imports the selected/current native leaf. Historical alternate
+  Claude branches are not emitted as separate resumable T3 threads; only the selected
+  leaf can safely preserve one native resume destination.
+- Provider-private context, encrypted reasoning and unavailable artifacts cannot
+  be reconstructed from public history APIs. The native provider owns continuation.
+  Delegation activity/results are retained; child conversations import separately.
+- Remote image URLs are represented only when the source provides inline bytes; the
+  importer does not fetch network resources during import.
+- A project’s historical Git branch, worktree checkout, uncommitted files, and
+  checkpoint blobs are not reconstructed. Continuation runs in the selected T3
+  project workspace, by design.
+- The `t3 import session` CLI requires a running-server URL, a scoped bearer token,
+  and a T3 project ID.
+- Claude's trailing tool activity after the last visible message is not imported; it
+  belongs to a turn that never produced a reply.
+- TodoWrite and ExitPlanMode calls import as tool items, not as plan artifacts.
+- Selected sessions have a 512 MiB selected-history memory budget, a 1,000,000-record
+  limit, and keep up to 100,000 messages; bulk discovery keeps its 32 MiB, 100,000-record,
+  and 200-message limits. Larger selected histories are skipped with a warning. The
+  budget counts selected fields, not the JSONL file size: the 364 MB target session
+  selects roughly 70 MB.
+
+## Verification command set
+
+From `apps/server`:
+
+```bash
+vp test run src/project/AgentSessionScanner.test.ts \
+  src/project/AgentSessionImporter.test.ts \
+  src/project/AgentSessionJson.test.ts \
+  src/orchestration-v2/Adapters/ClaudeAdapterV2.test.ts
+vp run typecheck
+```
+
+The focused suite covers Claude and native-provider import, including selected-history budgets, branch walks through unretained records,
+compaction, native pagination, snapshot checks, attachments, and provider binding.
+The server typecheck and production server/web build pass.
+
+These checks exercise the patched stable build. They do not patch an installed
+nightly or repair threads already imported there using `historyOrigin: "v1_import"`.
+
+Explicit native imports use provider APIs because raw file layouts are not a stable
+history contract: Codex can paginate or compress history, and OpenCode 2 projects
+its database through export. The raw scanner remains available for existing bulk
+imports. The native source service rejects partial/changing snapshots and mismatched
+instances/workspaces before projection. These checks are not a global writer lock;
+close other native CLI writers before importing.
